{"name":"Crystal Lake","hex":"#88b5c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crystal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid composed of an array of atoms or molecules possessing long-range order and arranged in a pattern which is periodic in three dimensions.","A piece of glimmering, shining mineral resembling ice or glass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of crystal.","Very clear; coherent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crystal"},{"term":"lake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, landlocked stretch of water or similar liquid.","A large amount of liquid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An offering, sacrifice, gift.","Play; sport; game; fun; glee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crystal Lake (Saskatchewan)","blocks":[{"text":"Crystal Lake is a lake straddling the boundary between the rural municipalities of Keys No. 303 and Buchanan No. 304 in eastern Saskatchewan, Canada. At 1.6 kilometres (0.99 mi) wide and 3.2 kilometres (2.0 mi) long, it is a small lake fed by natural underground springs. It is surrounded by the residential resort community of Crystal Lake. The lake is approximately 24 kilometres (15 mi) north of Canora and 24 kilometres (15 mi) south-east of Preeceville."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Crystal_Lake_View_from_East.jpg/330px-Crystal_Lake_View_from_East.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_Lake_(Saskatchewan)"},{"title":"Lynn River","blocks":[{"text":"The Lynn River is a fresh water river located in Norfolk County in Southwestern Ontario, Canada. It empties into Lake Erie at Port Dover."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynn_River"},{"title":"Crystal Lake (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Crystal Lake is an upcoming American slasher television series developed by Brad Caleb Kane that is based on the Friday the 13th film franchise. It is a prequel to the 1980 film and stars Linda Cardellini in the leading role of Pamela Voorhees, with Callum Vinson as a young Jason Voorhees, William Catlett, Devin Kessler, Cameron Scoggins and Gwendolyn Sundstrom."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_Lake_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Crystal","blocks":[{"text":"A crystal or crystalline solid is a solid material whose constituents are arranged in a highly ordered microscopic structure, forming a crystal lattice that extends in all directions. In addition, macroscopic single crystals are usually identifiable by their geometrical shape, consisting of flat faces with specific, characteristic orientations. The scientific study of crystals and crystal formation is known as crystallography. The process of crystal formation via mechanisms of crystal growth is called crystallization or solidification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Quartz_28.jpg/330px-Quartz_28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Lynn_River%2C_Ontario.jpg/500px-Lynn_River%2C_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Lynn_River%2C_Ontario.jpg/1280px-Lynn_River%2C_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Lynn_River%2C_Ontario.jpg/500px-Lynn_River%2C_Ontario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Lynn River in Port Dover.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALynn_River%2C_Ontario.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Sodium-chloride-3D-ionic.png/500px-Sodium-chloride-3D-ionic.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai